🚀 9. How to Run the Node (for Smart‑Contracts)
Your Rust contract engine runs inside the CosmaChain node.

Steps:
Start the Layer‑1 node  
From Layer1g-CosmaChain-Node

Code
cargo run
Build Smart‑Contracts

Code
cargo build
Run tests

Code
cargo test
Deploy domain contracts  
The dispatcher loads them automatically from contracts/.

Call contracts via SDK  
Layer3c App SDK →

Code
cosma.contracts.call("CosmaCareBooking", "create_booking", args)
🌟 10. Uniqueness & Advancement Summary
🔥 Has anything like this existed before?
Parts resemble:

Ethereum EVM

Solana runtime

Cosmos modules

Polkadot pallets

But none combine:

A Rust‑based contract VM

Identity‑bound transactions

Benefits agreements

Revenue splits

Gig‑economy domain contracts

Behavioral scoring (S3E2C3)

Economic scoring (ESEC)

Multi‑token benefits (CosmaCoin + SpotCoin)

Settlement logic for real‑world services

A unified dispatcher + ABI engine

🚀 Why this is an advancement in Web3
Layer1a is the first smart‑contract layer designed for real‑world 1099 workers, not DeFi speculation.

It enables:

Real service bookings

Real payouts

Real tax automation

Real identity verification

Real economic scoring

Real behavioral scoring

Real benefits distribution

This is Web3 for actual labor markets, not just finance.

Layer1a is the programmable benefits engine that powers CosmaTech.
